{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Filter continuation checkpoint. Refreshed origin/main at ce496143fe1f72a07efeb0173da37013262ec446 and confirmed a clean survey worktree. The approved F08 through F20 epic unhygenic-gabby-indianhare is closed. All eleven descendants are closed without force. Every repository change is reachable from origin/main, and the GitHub About change has an authenticated exact readback.\n\nRetained candidates under current evidence:\n\n- F14 will compare complete normalized server-manifest environment records from MCP_ENV_VARS. It will cover name, description, isRequired, and duplicate names without checking formatting, punctuation, or record order.\n- F15 will correct the synchronized adoption templates for seven relations and configuration-aware assignment guidance while preserving their byte-identical synchronization contract.\n- F16 will correct the static SVG directly, preserve its text-editable asset decision, and add title and description metadata without adding a generator or character checker.\n- F17 will correct assignment guidance and the unsigned fast-fail success claim in the example skills. The historical ticket arid-gutless-myna requires an append-only correction.\n- F18 is narrowed to the user guide. It will keep user commands and outcomes, add caused_by, and replace implementation or incident narration with links to maintained internal or operator documents. The lower README rewrite remains held pending a section ownership map.\n- F29 is narrowed to docs/your-first-change.md. It will replace direct hook download with make hooks, reserve recheck for proven environmental faults, direct nondeterministic tests to root-cause analysis, and require Gerrit for every change to main.\n- F31 is narrowed to stale writer attribution in docs/event-schema.md. It will replace deleted shell writers with current command or Python producer seams and remove the retired-writer footnote.\n- F38 is narrowed to docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md. It will correct the absolute module-size gate, remove machine-state claims and capture debris, and separate historical measurements from the maintained procedure.\n\nF20 requires a historical correction. Ticket aimless-seclusive-tigershark cites ADR 0018 as authority for enforceable plan review before claim. ADR 0018 governs T5c trust-boundary scoping. The proposed remedy is an append-only comment that points to docs/plan-review-gate.md and preserves the original ticket event.\n\nHeld items remain F23 and the lower README rewrite because neither proposal defines a complete maintained destination for displaced material. F30 remains pending reconciliation of RP-04 and RP-05 implementation state before any architecture label changes. Rejected F02, F03, and F04 remain excluded. Deferred F05 remains undecided. No project file changed during this filter checkpoint."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787502670044928001,"uuid":"3ad7a608-16dd-44a8-94fd-c29be439e32b"}